<title>BELGIUM: Solvay's Janssen to retire, Michielsen CEO.</title>
<headline>Solvay's Janssen to retire, Michielsen CEO.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian chemicals and drugs group Solvay said on Thursday its chief executive officer Daniel Janssen would retire in June 1998 to become chairman of the board.</p>
<p>New CEO would be Belgian Alois Michielsen.  </p>
<p>Michielsen was appointed vice-chairman of the executive committee in 1994, supervising the general management of Solvay's chemicals, plastics, processing and pharmaceuticals sectors as well as research and development.</p>
<p>-- Nieck Ammerlaan, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6816, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
